{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"quantitative_comparisons\": [\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"12-month PFS rate\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"d-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"70%\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"group\": \"p-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"41%\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"Median PFS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"d-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"24.0 months\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"group\": \"p-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"9.0 months\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"Median OS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"d-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"41.0 months\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"group\": \"p-FMT\",\n          \"value\": \"28.3 months\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MITRIC trial (P0578)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"All patients (n=12)\",\n          \"value\": \"0%\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MITRIC trial (P0578)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"Median PFS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"All patients (n=12)\",\n          \"value\": \"1.5 months\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MIMic trial (P0577)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"All patients (n=20)\",\n          \"value\": \"65%\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"MIMic trial (P0577)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"Median PFS\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"All patients (n=20)\",\n          \"value\": \"29.6 months\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"FMT-LUMINate (P0583)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2 single-arm, NSCLC\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"NSCLC cohort\",\n          \"value\": \"80%\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"research_object\": \"FMT-LUMINate (P0583)\",\n      \"result_or_measure\": \"ORR\",\n      \"setting_or_time\": \"Phase 2 single-arm, Melanoma\",\n      \"groups\": [\n        {\n          \"group\": \"Melanoma cohort\",\n          \"value\": \"75%\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usable_content\": \"当前提供的材料中未发现已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验（Phase III RCT）证实微生物干预在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。现有最高级别证据为 II 期或 IIa 期研究。TACITO 试验（P0593，2025 年发表）是一项随机、双盲、安慰剂对照的 IIa 期试验（n=45），在转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）一线治疗中，供体 FMT 组中位 PFS 显著优于安慰剂组（24.0 个月 vs 9.0 个月，HR=0.50，P=0.035），但主要终点 12 个月 PFS 率未达统计学显著性（70% vs 41%，P=0.053），总生存期（OS）差异亦不显著（P=0.167）。其他研究多为单臂早期试验：MITRIC 试验（P0578，IIa 期，n=12）在 ICI 耐药人群中未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%），中位 PFS 仅 1.5 个月；MIMic 试验（P0577，I 期，n=20）和 FMT-LUMINate（P0583，II 期）在一线或初治人群中报告了较高的 ORR（65%-80%）和生存数据，但缺乏随机对照设计。综述材料（P0584）明确指出截至其撰写时未发现完成的 III 期试验，并呼吁开展大规模标准化研究。因此，微生物干预的疗效信号主要来自 II 期及以下研究，且结果受人群（一线 vs 耐药）、癌种及方案异质性影响，尚未获得 III 期确证。\",\n  \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n  \"answers_requested_question\": false,\n  \"still_missing\": \"已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT 研究（如注册号为 NCT 开头的 III 期试验结果）。\",\n  \"read_focus\": \"\",\n  \"external_ask\": \"检索临床试验注册库（如 ClinicalTrials.gov）或最新文献，确认是否有已完成的微生物干预（FMT 或菌群制剂）联合 ICI 治疗实体瘤的 Phase III 随机对照试验及其主要结局数据（如 OS 或 PFS 的统计学显著性）。\",\n  \"reason\": \"问题要求确认是否存在已完成的 Phase III RCT。提供的材料中最高级别为 Phase 2a（TACITO），且多篇材料（P0584, P0577）明确说明当前缺乏 Phase III 数据。虽然材料强烈暗示目前尚无此类试验，但根据指令，确认“不存在”需要更广泛的检索（如注册库）以排除材料未覆盖的最新发表，因此不能仅凭现有材料宣布问题已解决（direct_use），需外部检索确认核心答案。\"\n}","reasoning_content":"The user is asking whether there are completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials (RCTs) confirming the efficacy of microbiome interventions (like FMT) in ICI-treated solid tumors.\n\nI need to check the provided materials for any mention of completed Phase III RCTs.\n\nMaterials provided:\n1.  **P0578 (MITRIC trial):** Single-arm Phase IIa basket trial. Not Phase III, not randomized. Results: ORR 0%, limited efficacy in ICI-refractory patients.\n2.  **P0593 (TACITO trial):** Investigator-initiated, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled **Phase 2a** trial. Published 2025. Evaluated FMT in mRCC. Primary endpoint (12-month PFS rate) not statistically met (P=0.053), but median PFS improved. Not Phase III.\n3.  **P0594 (Kim et al.):** Prospective, single-arm, single-center study (2024). Not Phase III, not randomized.\n4.  **P0577 (MIMic trial):** Phase I multicenter trial (single-arm). Mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17). No Phase III data.\n5.  **P0583 (FMT-LUMINate):** Phase 2 trial (open-label, single-arm for reported cohorts). Mentions CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461) but does not report results or confirm completion as Phase III.\n6.  **P0584 (Narrative Review):** Explicitly states \"no completed large randomised phase III trial... was identified\". Calls for future large-scale RCTs.\n\nAnalysis:\n-   None of the provided materials report a completed **Phase III** RCT.\n-   The most advanced trial mentioned is TACITO (P0593), which is Phase 2a.\n-   Several materials explicitly state the lack of Phase III data (P0584, P0577, P0583).\n-   The question asks \"Is there a completed large-scale Phase III RCT...?\"\n-   Based on these materials, the answer is **No** (or at least, none are reported in this set).\n-   However, I must be careful not to overgeneralize. The materials say *they* didn't find one or *this* study isn't one. P0584 explicitly says \"no completed large randomised phase III trial... was identified in this material\".\n-   The success criteria require finding a published Phase III RCT with primary outcome data.\n-   Since none of the materials provide this, `answers_requested_question` should be `false` regarding the *existence* of such a trial based *only* on these materials, but I can state that the materials indicate none exist *up to the time of these publications*.\n-   Actually, if the question is \"Is there...\", and the materials say \"No Phase III trials found/reported\", I can answer \"Based on current provided literature, no Phase III RCTs have been reported.\" But strictly speaking, to confirm a negative globally requires external search. However, for the purpose of the review based on *these* materials, the finding is that evidence is currently at Phase I/II.\n-   Decision: `external_research` is appropriate because confirming the *absence* of Phase III trials globally usually requires a registry search or broader systematic review beyond these specific papers, but the materials themselves provide strong evidence that the field is currently in Phase I/II.\n-   Wait, the instruction says: \"For questions like 'has there been X research/result', finding one instance that fits can answer it. If several papers don't mention it, or an earlier review says none existed then, it cannot answer whether it exists now.\"\n-   P0593 is published in 2025. It calls itself Phase 2a.\n-   P0584 is a review that says no Phase III found.\n-   So, based *strictly* on these materials, I cannot definitively say \"No Phase III exists in the world\", but I can say \"No Phase III results are reported in these sources, the latest being 2025\".\n-   The `success_criteria` is \"Find a published Phase III RCT...\". I have not found one. So `answers_requested_question` = `false`.\n-   `decision` = `external_research` because I need to confirm if a Phase III exists outside these papers (e.g., registry search), although the materials suggest none exist yet.\n-   `usable_content` should summarize the highest level of evidence found (Phase 2a/2) and explicitly state the lack of Phase III data as reported in these texts.\n\nQuantitative Comparisons:\n-   P0578 (MITRIC): Phase IIa, Single-arm. n=12. ORR 0%. mPFS 1.5 months. mOS 10.1 months.\n-   P0593 (TACITO): Phase 2a, RCT. n=45. 12-month PFS rate: 70% (d-FMT) vs 41% (p-FMT), P=0.053. Median PFS: 24.0 vs 9.0 months, HR=0.50, P=0.035. Median OS: 41.0 vs 28.3 months, P=0.167.\n-   P0577 (MIMic): Phase I, Single-arm. n=20. ORR 65%. mPFS 29.6 months. mOS 52.8 months.\n-   P0583 (FMT-LUMINate): Phase 2, Single-arm (reported). NSCLC ORR 80%, Melanoma ORR 75%.\n\nI need to structure `usable_content` to highlight that while Phase 2 data exists (some randomized), Phase 3 is missing.\n\nPlan:\n1.  Extract quantitative data for the trials mentioned (MITRIC, TACITO, MIMic, FMT-LUMINate).\n2.  Write `usable_content` stating the current evidence level (Phase I/II), highlighting TACITO as the only randomized Phase 2a with positive PFS signal but missed primary endpoint, and explicitly noting the absence of Phase III data in these sources.\n3.  Set `decision` to `external_research` because the core question (existence of Phase III) is not confirmed positively, and confirming the negative requires broader search than just these papers (though they suggest negative).\n4.  `answers_requested_question` = `false` (Success criteria not met).\n\nLet's refine `quantitative_comparisons`.\n-   TACITO (P0593):\n    -   Group: d-FMT, 12-month PFS rate: 70%\n    -   Group: p-FMT, 12-month PFS rate: 41%\n    -   Group: d-FMT, Median PFS: 24.0 months\n    -   Group: p-FMT, Median PFS: 9.0 months\n    -   Group: d-FMT, Median OS: 41.0 months\n    -   Group: p-FMT, Median OS: 28.3 months\n-   MITRIC (P0578):\n    -   Group: All patients (n=12), ORR: 0%\n    -   Group: All patients, mPFS: 1.5 months\n    -   Group: All patients, mOS: 10.1 months\n-   MIMic (P0577):\n    -   Group: All patients (n=20), ORR: 65%\n    -   Group: All patients, mPFS: 29.6 months\n    -   Group: All patients, mOS: 52.8 months\n-   FMT-LUMINate (P0583):\n    -   Group: NSCLC cohort, ORR: 80%\n    -   Group: Melanoma cohort, ORR: 75%\n\nI will focus on TACITO as it's the only RCT mentioned, but clarify it's Phase 2a.\n\n`usable_content` needs to be a string.\n`decision` needs to be one of `direct_use`, `local_deep_read`, `external_research`.\nSince the question asks \"Is there...\", and I haven't found one, but the materials suggest there isn't, I should flag `external_research` to confirm the *current* status beyond these specific papers (e.g. clinical trial registries), as papers might lag. However, P0593 is 2025, which is very recent. It still says Phase 2a. So it's likely true there is no Phase 3. But to be rigorous per instructions: \"For 'whether there is already X research' questions, finding one instance... can answer. Several papers not mentioning... cannot answer current existence.\"\nSo I must say `external_research` to confirm the negative definitively, but I can report the materials' statement that none were found.\n\nActually, the instruction says: \"If still need to confirm whether target research appeared later, choose external_research... do not announce problem solved while still requesting confirmation of core answer.\"\nSo `decision` = `external_research`. `answers_requested_question` = `false`.\n\nLet's draft the content.","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":13870,"completion_tokens":3688,"total_tokens":17558,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2104,"text_tokens":3688},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text